# Scan the commit message itself.
#
# scan-pii.sh reads `git ls-files` and scan-text.sh reads a drafted file, so a
# commit message was the one outbound surface neither of them saw. An audit
# found personal data in published commit messages, including in the messages
# of commits whose whole purpose was removing it from the files. A commit
# message is as public as the diff; it gets the same gate.
#
# $1 is the path to the message file, which is exactly what scan-text.sh takes.
bash scripts/scan-text.sh "$1"
